<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Jean-François Allard</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1785">1785</a>–<a href="/years/1839">1839</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a> · Also known as Allard</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Jean-François Allard was a French former officer of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/napoleon">Napoleon</a>'s armies who entered the service of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ranjit-singh">Ranjit Singh</a>. He organised and trained cavalry units of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sikhism">Sikh</a> army on European lines. He is remembered as one of the European officers who modernised the military of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sikh-empire">Sikh Empire</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/jean-francois-allard.jpg" alt="Jean-François Allard" width="320" height="416" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Joseph-Désiré Court · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Painting_of_Jean-Fran%C3%A7ois_Allard,_by_Joseph-D%C3%A9sir%C3%A9_Court,_1837.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
